Hi Talel

On 06.11.23 at 11:46, BELHADJ SALEM Talel wrote:
> Hi Michael,
>
> Regarding the comment dotted boxes, in draw.io <http://draw.io> they 
> have the full multi-line content as shown also in docs html view,
> but Inkscape replaces half of the content with "...", I don't know 
> why. I am not experienced with Inkscape.

I tried a few things with draw.io but this didn't help: the output stays 
the same, incompatible with Inkscape.

Anyway, we shouldn't expect contributors to the Yocto Project to have to 
get familiar with proprietary software such as draw.io if they want to 
modify the diagrams (even if it is provided free of charge for the 
moment). It would indeed help if you learned to modify your diagram 
directly with Inkscape, to guarantee that future contributors can use 
such software too.

Also look at the output SVG, and compare He with the clean one produced 
by Inkscape in overview-manual/svg/git-workflow.svg. It looks much 
cleaner and you may even make string changes directly with a text 
editor. This reminds me of HTML code generated by MS Word in the 2000's 
(maybe that's still the same), vs the code a human would write. Quality 
is another difference between proprietary and free software.

Actually, I checked and it seems it's not complicated to fix the 
multi-line text boxes by hand in Inkscape. Just put the cursor at the 
end of the line, press [Enter] or [Shift][Enter] and you can add the 
remaining text back. Even though you'll have to type it again.

I hope you can do it.
Thanks in advance
Cheers
Michael.

